xfce4-caramos-plugin (1.1.0) noble; urgency=medium

  * Show desktop (caramos-show-desktop): a strip 4 pixels wide, the height of
    the panel, at the very end of the CaramOS Xfce taskbar, after the right
    island (tickets H-1189 and H-1192). It shows a thin line when the pointer
    is on it; a click hides every window and shows the desktop, a second
    click brings them back (_NET_SHOWING_DESKTOP), as Super+D does. Xfce's
    own Show Desktop plugin is as wide as the panel is high, which would move
    the island away from the edge of the screen. An internal plugin: no
    process of its own.

 -- Vietnam Linux Family <developer@vietnamlinuxfamily.net>  Tue, 24 Nov 2026 10:00:00 +0700

xfce4-caramos-plugin (1.0.0) noble; urgency=medium

  * The CaramOS Control Center button for the Xfce panel: an XEmbed socket in
    the taskbar's right island, where caramos-ota's Control Center draws its
    button and opens its popup.

